  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Brand Perception Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"A brand perception survey asks people how they see a brand: the words they link to it, how it rates on statements such as fair pricing, and how it compares with rivals. Run on a schedule, it shows whether that view is moving.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"Decide who to ask, write four to six attribute statements, and put an open first-word question ahead of them. Then add the same statements for two rivals. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns that outline into a working survey with its own answer table.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the purpose of brand perception surveys?\", \"a\": \"Sales figures show what people buy. Brand perception surveys show which traits buyers credit you with and where a rival is rated higher. Repeated on a schedule, they also tell you whether a pricing or service change moved the score.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should be in a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"Strong brand perception survey questions cover the first word that comes to mind, agreement with attribute statements, and a comparison with named rivals. Open with one screening question so you know who is answering. Service quality for current buyers belongs in a customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a brand perception survey include?\", \"a\": \"Count the attribute statements first, since each one repeats for every rival. Four statements across your brand and two rivals already make 12 ratings, before the screener and the first-word question. Each statement you add costs three more ratings. Keep only those a decision depends on.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a brand perception survey include competitors?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Pick the two or three that buyers weigh against you, and rate each on the statements you use for your own brand. A drop shared by every brand in the category points to the market. A drop that hits only yours points back at something you changed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a brand perception survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A working brand perception survey template opens with a screening question and the open word question, then five attribute statements repeated for each rival. Describe your brand and two competitors to Emergent, and it builds that structure with every response stored in your own database.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good brand perception survey examples?\", \"a\": \"A quarterly tracker that rates a bank against two rivals is one. A split test where each shopper sees a single package design is another. Candidates can rate a hiring process too, while staff views of the company fit an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you send brand perception surveys?\", \"a\": \"Quarterly works for a brand that changes prices or campaigns often, and twice a year is enough in a slower category. Hold whichever cadence you choose, because a trend line needs evenly spaced points. To read a launch, add a separate wave instead of moving a regular one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many responses should a brand perception survey collect?\", \"a\": \"Size each wave for the smallest group you plan to report on, not for the total. A wave of 400 split across four regions leaves about 100 per region, thin for a score you mean to act on. Emergent puts no cap on responses, which leaves sample size a fieldwork call, never a plan limit.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}